Usages:
  confchange_validation: |
    Every topology mutation (AddMember, RemoveMember, UpdateRaftAttributes, PromoteMember) is
    driven by a raft ConfChange entry and must pass validation (id not already removed/existing,
    peer URL not already in use, learner-count ceiling not exceeded) before being applied to the
    in-memory RaftCluster and persisted.

Annotations: |
  This cell owns the cluster's topology model: the set of `Member`s (their raft peer URLs,
  learner status, client URLs, names) and the cluster ID/version, encapsulated in `RaftCluster`.
  It persists that state through its own backend interface (not documented as a separate cell
  here) rather than importing a storage cell directly. It is a leaf relative to this forest:
  nothing else documented here is a dependency of this cell.

  Use `confchange_validation` before adding new mutation entry points.

---

"RaftCluster()":
  location: cluster.go
  annotations: |
    A list of `Member`s that belong to the same raft cluster, plus cluster ID and
    storage-version metadata. Mutated only through confchange-validated operations driven by
    etcdserver as it applies raft configuration changes.
  methods:
    "Members() -> members:[]Member": |
      Return every known member, in a stable, deterministic order.
    "Member(id uint64) -> member:Member": |
      Look up one member by raft ID; returns nil if unknown.
    "IsIDRemoved(id uint64) -> removed:bool": |
      True if `id` was once a member and has since been removed; removed IDs are never reused.
    "PeerURLs() -> urls:[]string": |
      All peer (raft-transport) URLs across every member, used by the raft transport cell to
      know which addresses to dial.
    "ClientURLs() -> urls:[]string": |
      All client-facing URLs across every member.
    "AddMember(member Member)": |
      Add `member` to the cluster and persist it, after confchange validation has already
      passed.

      Algorithm:
      1. Reject if `member`'s ID was previously removed or already exists
      2. Reject if any of `member`'s peer URLs collide with an existing member
      3. Insert into the in-memory member set and persist via the backend interface
    "RemoveMember(id uint64)": |
      Remove the member identified by `id`, mark its ID as permanently removed, and persist the
      change.
    "UpdateRaftAttributes(id uint64, peerURLs []string)": |
      Update the peer URLs of an existing member (e.g. after a peer's address changes).
    "PromoteMember(id uint64)": |
      Convert a learner member into a full voting member once it has caught up sufficiently.
    "Recover(onSet OnVersionSetFunc)": |
      Reload cluster state from the backend at startup, invoking `onSet` once the cluster
      version has been determined.

"Member()":
  location: member.go
  annotations: |
    One cluster member: its raft ID, peer URLs (for raft transport), client URLs (for client
    traffic), human-readable name, and learner status.
  properties:
    "ID -> uint64": |
      Unique raft member ID, stable for the member's lifetime.
    "PeerURLs -> []string": |
      URLs other members use to reach this member's raft transport.
    "ClientURLs -> []string": |
      URLs clients use to reach this member's client-facing API.
    "IsLearner -> bool": |
      True if this member is a non-voting learner (catching up before promotion) rather than a
      full voting member.
  methods:
    "Clone() -> member:Member": |
      Return a deep copy, safe to mutate independently of the original.

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  Cluster topology model (membership, peer/client URLs, learner status). Consumed by the raft
  transport cell (to know peer addresses) and the gRPC adapter cell (to answer member-list/
  member-add requests); leaf relative to this forest.
